<title>USA: Red Clay, Del., schools reject $23.7 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Red Clay, Del., schools reject $23.7 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters in Wilmington, Del., on Tuesday rejected a $23.7 million bond ballot for capital improvements for the Red Clay School District.</p>
<p>The vote was 7,282 to 5,086, according to a school district official.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
